{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115628",
      "title": "When (Not) To Rely On Host Elements",
      "lectureOrder": 116,
      "videoOrder": 110,
      "sourceHash": "bf99ca7ea6375e1c3c1d8a805e7cda74fa2b48927e88542c49043bae1dfeb8cd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.82,
          "en": "Now this host property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.82,
          "end": 5.07,
          "en": "which can be added to @Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.07,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "can be useful as I explained, because we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 12.513,
          "en": "also use it somewhere else in our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.5,
          "end": 15.423,
          "en": "on the dashboard item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.77,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "In the dashboard item template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 22.02,
          "en": "I have that div with the class dashboard item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.02,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "And this is a bit redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 27.513,
          "en": "We don't need that extra wrapper around this article.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.86,
          "end": 33.86,
          "en": "So what we could do is remove it here from our template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 39.15,
          "en": "and we could now go to the dashboard item component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.15,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "TypeScript file and add host here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 46.53,
          "en": "And then again, use that setting to add the class property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 51.033,
          "en": "to the host element, so to this app-dashboard-item element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.93,
          "end": 55.08,
          "en": "and set it to a value of dashboard-item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.08,
          "end": 58.323,
          "en": "or whichever CSS class you want to add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 60.9,
          "en": "And if you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.9,
          "end": 64.293,
          "en": "you'll see that your application looks broken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "Well, it is now broken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 70.92,
          "en": "because of course in the dashboard item CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.92,
          "end": 72.66,
          "en": "I'm still setting up styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.66,
          "end": 75.36,
          "en": "that are scoped to this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "so that only look for matches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 79.233,
          "en": "inside of the component template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 83.61,
          "en": "So if I'm looking for an element with a CSS class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "of dashboard-item on it, Angular will only look for it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "in this component's template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "And here we have no such element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 94.68299999999999,
          "en": "with that class on it anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 100.02000000000001,
          "en": "Sure, that class exists on the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.02000000000001,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "and you can confirm that it was added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.75999999999999,
          "en": "by inspecting this on the running page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.75999999999999,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "Here on app dashboard item, you find that class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 112.38,
          "en": "but it is ignored because of that style scoping,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 114.363,
          "en": "because of that encapsulation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.62,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "So of course we could disable encapsulation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 123.06,
          "en": "by setting encapsulation to view encapsulation non,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.06,
          "end": 125.61,
          "en": "as we did it for a control component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 128.01,
          "en": "or we go for a different approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.01,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "which is what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 133.11,
          "en": "Nonetheless, I wanted to highlight that you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.11,
          "end": 136.35,
          "en": "that host property to any component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.35,
          "end": 140.25,
          "en": "not just components without view encapsulation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.25,
          "end": 142.2,
          "en": "Here for this specific use case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.2,
          "end": 145.41,
          "en": "it just won't work the way you want it to work maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.41,
          "end": 150.06,
          "en": "But if you were to add any other property, like maybe an id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.06,
          "end": 152.25,
          "en": "then you could absolutely do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 154.023,
          "en": "through that host property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.07,
          "end": 156.54,
          "en": "But here for this use case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.54,
          "end": 159.63,
          "en": "host is not a tool that will help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.63,
          "end": 164.63,
          "en": "Instead, to style the host element of this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "we should go to the dashboard item component CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 172.59,
          "en": "and use another feature about which you learned earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.59,
          "end": 175.983,
          "en": "In here, you can use the :host selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 181.62,
          "en": "and replace all dashboard-item class occurrences with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.62,
          "end": 183.273,
          "en": "also here in the media query.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.57,
          "end": 189.3,
          "en": "And with that, we got back our styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.3,
          "end": 191.28,
          "en": "and it looks the way it did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.28,
          "end": 194.283,
          "en": "but now again, using this host element styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 198.9,
          "en": "Of course, we can now also revisit the other components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.9,
          "end": 203.64,
          "en": "and see if we can get rid of some unnecessary wrappers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.64,
          "end": 205.59,
          "en": "For example, in server-status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.59,
          "end": 208.263,
          "en": "there I also have that div with that id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.31,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "We could delete that, that div with that id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 217.173,
          "en": "so that I just have this conditional statement in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 221.16,
          "en": "And then in server-status.component.CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 225.78,
          "en": "I'll replace all those is selectors with :host.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.78,
          "end": 229.07999999999998,
          "en": "And by the way, there are certain rules in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.07999999999998,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "which won't have any effect yet, but we'll change this soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.64,
          "end": 238.38,
          "en": "For the moment, I'll just replace my id selector with :host.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.38,
          "end": 241.053,
          "en": "And it turns out I only had one in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 246.03,
          "en": "Now, here in the new-ticket.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 246.03,
          "end": 249,
          "en": "we could get rid of that form element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 249,
          "end": 253.29,
          "en": "and rely on our component host element as a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 253.29,
          "end": 255.36,
          "en": "around these input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 255.36,
          "end": 258.93,
          "en": "But the built in form element is an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 258.93,
          "end": 262.2,
          "en": "I don't wanna remove here because it makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 262.2,
          "end": 266.85,
          "en": "to have it for semantic and accessibility reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.85,
          "end": 270.18,
          "en": "Our custom component host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 270.18,
          "end": 272.67,
          "en": "won't tell the browser anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 272.67,
          "end": 275.61,
          "en": "won't tell screen readers anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 275.61,
          "end": 278.55,
          "en": "and therefore you typically wanna avoid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.55,
          "end": 283.23,
          "en": "getting rid of semantically important elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 283.23,
          "end": 286.32,
          "en": "It's different for things like divs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 286.32,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "which have no semantic meaning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 293.04,
          "en": "but forms, buttons, sections and things like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 293.04,
          "end": 296.82,
          "en": "you might want to consider keeping those as wrappers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 296.82,
          "end": 298.86,
          "en": "instead of replacing them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.86,
          "end": 301.893,
          "en": "with your component host element as a wrapper.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.48,
          "end": 306.18,
          "en": "In the ticket.component, I don't have any markup yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 306.18,
          "end": 309.13,
          "en": "We didn't work on that yet, so I'll leave it the way it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 310.14,
          "end": 312.12,
          "en": "In the tickets.component, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 312.12,
          "end": 314.13,
          "en": "I do want to make a change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 314.13,
          "end": 316.71,
          "en": "because in the tickets.component.CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 316.71,
          "end": 320.4,
          "en": "I now want a target host here instead of an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.4,
          "end": 323.73,
          "en": "with id tickets, which doesn't exist yet anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 323.73,
          "end": 327.96,
          "en": "because that will help us later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 327.96,
          "end": 332.26,
          "en": "So here on all my rules, I'm targeting the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 335.4,
          "end": 336.72,
          "en": "In the traffic.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 336.72,
          "end": 339.79,
          "en": "I'll get rid of that div with id traffic here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 342.48,
          "end": 347.48,
          "en": "and instead again, target :host just as we did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 351.87,
          "end": 354.39,
          "en": "And with that, if I save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 354.39,
          "end": 357,
          "en": "it again looks the way it did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 357,
          "end": 359.7,
          "en": "but now we're taking advantage of the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 359.7,
          "end": 362.58,
          "en": "that Angular does render that host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 362.58,
          "end": 366.243,
          "en": "and that allows us to avoid unnecessary wrappers.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
